    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office opened in 1897, marking Yancey's early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/yancey-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1914, Yancey boasted 350 residents, two general stores, a drug store, a cotton gin, a blacksmith shop, and was famed for peaches, plums, and its “Yancey watermelons.”.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/yancey-tx",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1924, Yancey’s economy was almost entirely based on the soil, producing cattle, hogs, goats, corn, cotton, honey, broomcorn, and sorghum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/yancey-tx",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The community school system consolidated into a single central school in 1912, pioneering vocational agriculture and home economics in Medina County.",
